==English==

===Etymology===
Partly from {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|headway|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|hēafodweġ||head-road, main-road}}, equivalent to {{prefix|head|way}}; partly as a shortening of {{term|ahead-way|lang=en}}, the source of the nautical sense.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|headways}}

# [[movement|Movement]] ahead or forward.
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} [[forward|Forward]] [[motion]], or its [[rate]].
# {{context|countable|transport|lang=en}} The [[interval]] of [[time]] or [[distance]] between the fronts of two [[vehicles]] (e.g. [[bus]]es) moving in succession in the same [[direction]], especially along the same pre-determined [[route]].
# {{context|uncountable|figuratively|lang=en}} [[progress|Progress]] toward a [[goal]].
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} The [[clearance]] beneath an object, such as an [[arch]], [[ceiling]] or [[bridge]]; [[headroom]].
# {{context|coal-mining|lang=en}} A [[cross-heading]].

